A||N||6||watdge||87 GT for sale, my 1st fiero if I buy it, your opinions please... ||||5||
Z||000000||watdge||03-25-2001||11:44 PM||||Hey all, have a look please:<P>   The white 87 GT has been for sale for about 2 weeks now and I believe that the a few folks have gone by to look at the car.  I'm looking at buying it as my first car.  I'm 16 years old don't exactly have a massive budget.  I really like the styling and such.  The owner is asking $4k for it and says that it only has 68k miles on it.  But there is something rather strange about this car.  Some folks have told me at school that Len, the owner, has had some trouble with the car from time to time.  It left him stranded at a stoplight once I believe.  On top of that, the carfax report on it says:  <P>"EXCEEDS MECHANICAL LIMITS TITLE ISSUED"<BR>(This was the title description used in 1997 and in 2000)  I'll send the actual report if you would like to see it.<P>I.E.:  Odometer Rollover-&gt; 168,000 Miles on the car<P><BR>   Now, from my opinion, the car looks like it's in good condition.  Though, one thing that has caught my attention, which is on the front bumper, that may give a clue to why that title was given.  The paint has a few "spider webs", not major, but noticable from close.  There are also a few round scratches about the size of a corn kernal each in a small cluster... maybe 4 dots.  Anyway, it appears as if the car's original color was maroon or burgandy color and it has been painted white as a new color (which could explain the spider webs).  I would give you a few photos but my digital camera battery is dead and I couldn't find another lithium battery lieing around.  As for the interior, nice (for a 14 1/2 year old car.  My dad's car is a '90 Ford Taurus with 170k miles, and it's dash is cracked all over the place and is in a whole lot worst condition than the older fiero.  And my dad's car isn't hardly worth $1000).  The dash looks like the car came out a year ago, condition wise.  No torn seats, no cracked dash, the floor mats are not discolored or dark around the petals, the guages are clean and not dusted or dirty *probably well detailed*, new shifter, AC/heat works, new clutch *I think the owner now was planning on Autocross, or at least he said he was* there are cracks it appears in some places in the plastic, there's a small one on the spoiler's support arm and a few small cracks here and there on the rest of the car.  Nothing deep.. but separation is noticable from 5 feet away.  He's got a nice CD player and speaker setup.  I haven't seen how it runs yet or how it drives.. so I'll probably do that soon.  I think that a while back when I first talked to him and he first got the car 3 months ago, that the car was having trouble shifting into certain gears.. such as first when stopped or something like that, I think that's correct, anyway, I haven't heard him complain of the problem since he's got the new clutch so--*shrug*.  It's also got a "super chip" which along with a few other small mods such as a high flow cat, which he did himself, a 160 degree thermostat, K/N filter which "gives the car about 190HP" (not sure if that's possible with his mods), that's what the guy says at least. It's got the black honey combed rims and a very firm suspension (it only rebounds back up, no bouncing when pushed down).  It was just in the shop recently because it wouldn't start.  But according to a good friend of the owner that the altenator *sp?* belt had gone bad, so he replaced the battery and I think the belt.  As for the rest of the car, I believe it's in great shape.  But then again, I'm not really sure to believe Carfax or the guy.  I mean, if the engine turns up being sour, then so be it, but I'd really not like to have an expensive lesson like that.  I had originally planed on replacing the engine eventually with a 3.4 liter then applying a turbo  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">, but for the time being, I just want a car that will get me from point A to point B with style, performance, and confidence.  As I said before, the guy is asking $4k for it,  which, if the car has 168,000 miles on it.. well--I don't think it would exactly be worth $4.  I thought about offering $3k for it before I saw the Title report.  But I'm not sure, if that's the case, is $2000 or $1500 a good price for the car?  Should I consider anything else beside the test drive and fluid check?  And if you were in my shoes, would you end up buying the car, and if so, at what price?  Oh well, I know I just spit out a lot of info, but thanks for your time and for listening, the car just excites me.  I've always wanted a car that is just all around great performance and handling, I just never knew that the Fiero was the answer until about a year ago.  Once I found this forum, it was as if I got prefiero fever <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">, I really like the cars.  I'm sure I'll love the car even more whether it's that 87GT or another fiero if I end up getting one.  Your input would be great, thanks in advance.<P>Jeremy *undoubtable future owner of a Fiero <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">*<P>I'll see if I can get pictures in for ya'll soon.||||reg||5
Z||000001||watdge||03-26-2001||12:02 AM||||Sorry, I forgot to mention, I believe Len bought it for $4000 about 3 months back.<p>[This message has been edited by watdge (edited 03-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tweek||03-26-2001||12:11 AM||||Now... on my '84, and alos other dash pics I have seen, there are 6 digits to the odometer (not counting tenths if they are there) Which means, if it truely DOES have 168K then by looking at it, it should read 168xxx miles. Only cars with 5 digits can qualify for "EXCEEDS MECHANICAL LIMITS" because once they reach 100,000 miles it starts at 0 again. A Fiero wont do that until 1 Million miles. IF it does have 68K I think 3K would be a fair price. <BR>Cheers.<P>-Ted||||reg||1
Z||000003||watdge||03-26-2001||12:33 AM||||Well that's good to hear.  Strange that carfax would screw up.. maybe it was just a problem with the titlest or something.  Thanks for informing me of that.  I couldn't get a good glance at the odometer, so I went by the paper in the window. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>What do you other folks think is a reasonable price... or is the car not worthy of being bought?<P>------------------<BR>Performance Enthusiest,<BR>Jeremy||||reg||14
Z||000004||Hank is Here||03-26-2001||12:47 AM||||I would say 4K sounds a little high for the car.  I would offer about 2500 .   Probably 3 would be on the upper end, the bonus is the low milage.||||reg||1
Z||000005||watdge||03-26-2001||07:54 PM||||Found out today that Len, the owner of the car is a detailer for a dodge dealership in the area.. that would explain the nice interior.  Also.. I found that yeah, the odometer has 6 digits.. but, one of thoses digits is for the 10th's of a mile.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> and thus.. leaves the odometer to only read up to 100,000 before rolling over.  I think there may have been some confusion about that.  But from the pictures I looked at.. I only saw a 6 digit cluster odometer, 5 if you take out the white 10th of a mile counter.  Also, I was told today that the car has a newer engine in it.  The owner didn't tell me that, but one of his friends did.  *shrug*  I'll talk to him later on this evening, so any other input would be great!<P>------------------<BR>Performance Enthusiest,<BR>Jeremy||||reg||14
Z||000006||87GTZ34||03-27-2001||01:20 AM||||I agree with Hank.  Offer $2500 and work up a 'little'. I just paid $2700 for and '87 GT which had 65K on 2.8 rebuild.  It needed brakes all the way around, a passenger axle, manifold was cracked, and valve job. I paid too much as I didn't hear the miss from the burned valve (probably due to the manifold tick).  Fortunately for me, I do my own work otherwise I'd be in trouble on this one.  Ask for service records for things like brakes, suspension parts, eng trans & clutch (the biggies).  Good luck and if this one doesn't work out there are more out there.||||reg||1
